  "notes": "Source: official Aquinas College pre-health advising page (AQUINAS.EDU/academics/biology-and-health-science/pre-health.html), 'Biology Major Four-Year Plan for Pre-Veterinary students'. Term-by-term sequence transcribed verbatim: 8 semesters, 122 credits; every printed semester-credit header reconciles with its course credits. Catalog year recorded as 2020-2021: the plan's course codes match the official 2020-2021 Aquinas College Academic Catalog (https://AQUINAS.EDU/_files/Academic-Catalog-2020-2021.pdf) — BY328 Genetics (WI) 5.0, BY170 Introduction to Organisms 4.0, BY171 Introduction to Cells 4.0, BY221 Anatomy and Histology of Vertebrates 4.0, BY231 Microbiology 4.0, BY326 Cell Biology 4.0, BY350 Evolution 4.0, BY372 Physiology 4.0, BY499 Senior Seminar 3.0 (SC). The 2021-2022 catalog renumbered Genetics to BY228 and the 2025-2026 catalog renumbered all biology courses to the BIO prefix, so the plan page (whose content reflects the older numbering) is pinned to 2020-2021. Course titles and prerequisites come from the 2020-2021 catalog course descriptions; where the plan page abbreviates a title, the catalog's official title is used (BY171 'Introduction to Cells' — page prints 'Introduction to Organisms'; BY221 'Anatomy and Histology of Vertebrates' — page prints 'Comparative Anatomy'; BY499 'Senior Seminar' — page prints 'Senior Seminar (SC)'; MS114 'Precalculus' — page prints 'College Algebra & Trigonometry'; GE100 'First Year Experience: College in the 21st Century' — page prints 'First Year Experience'; GE203 'Question Everything: Research as Inquiry' — page prints 'Research as Inquiry'; PC201 'General Physics: Mechanics, Sound, Heat' and PC202 'General Physics: Electricity, Magnetism, Light, Nuclear Physics' — page prints 'General Physics I/II'). Prerequisite notes: (1) BY350 requires the introductory biology sequence plus one upper-level biology course; encoded with BY372, an in-plan upper-level course taken before it. (2) PH244 lists 'PH101 or instructor permission' as prerequisite; PH101 (Introduction to Philosophy: Know Thyself, an HP course) is carried in external_prereqs and can fill the History-or-Philosophy general-education slot. (3) BY231 Microbiology is offered every spring and is placed in sophomore spring, consistent with the catalog. (4) BY299 'Animal Nutrition (Online Transfer)' is printed verbatim on the plan page as a transfer course; BY299 is not an Aquinas catalog course, so it carries no catalog prereq and is transcribed exactly as the official plan prints it. (5) BY499 requires senior status and instructor permission (senior status met: 106+ credits precede the final spring). WL101/WL102 are the required first-year world-language sequence slots (page prints 'Foreign Language I/II'); the student chooses the language. The plan assumes no prior college credits from dual enrollment or credit by exam (per page). The 2020-2021 Biology major is a Bachelor of Science (57 semester hours). total_credits equals the sum of ALL semester course credits including choice slots, matching the printed plan total of 122.",
